{"result":"{
  "id": "19105",
  "key": "SFCC-689",
  "summary": "Regional Storefronts — EU Language Mismatch Modal",
  "url": "https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/rest/api/2/issue/19105",
  "description": "As a Shopper browsing the EU Domestic storefront, \nI want to be prompted to switch to my preferred language when my detected language does not match the EU URL I have landed on, \nso that I can shop in the language most relevant to me.\n\n----\n\nThis story covers the EU language mismatch prompt on the EU Domestic storefront only. It is triggered on first visit when the shopper's browser-detected language does not match the language of the EU locale URL they have landed on (e.g. a French-speaking visitor lands on /es-eu/).\n\nThe underlying PWA component (`global/country-language-mismatch`, Language Prompt Banner variant) is built in SFCC-831 and consumed here.\n\nImage for reference (Figma leading): \n\n![\"image-20260827-032928.png\"](image-20260827-032928.png)",
