content.content:
{"result":"{
  "id": "19314",
  "key": "SFCC-817",
  "customfield_10231": {
    "value": "1. Given a visitor arrives at the Zimmermann site for the first time, when their IP address is detected and maps to a country in the Country List per Storefront, then the system automatically routes them to the assigned regional storefront for that country without requiring any manual action.\n2. Given a visitor's IP address maps to an Oceania region country (per the Country List), when they arrive on site, then they are routed to the AU storefront (ZimmermannAU).\n3. Given a visitor's IP address maps to an Oceania region country, when they attempt to access any non-AU storefront URL directly, then they are redirected to the AU storefront.\n4. Given a visitor's IP address does not map to an Oceania region country, when they attempt to access the AU storefront URL directly, then they are blocked and redirected to the storefront assigned to their detected country per the Country List.\n5. Given a returning visitor who has previously dismissed the country mismatch slide-out or made a manual country selection, when they return to the site, then IP-based auto-routing does not override their saved preference.\n6. Given the IP geolocation service is unavailable or returns an unrecognised result, when a visitor arrives on site, then they are routed to the fallback storefront without error (fallback storefront TBC — see dependencies)."
  }
}"}

